<title>GERMANY: Second German beet test shows higher sugar yield.</title>
<headline>Second German beet test shows higher sugar yield.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The second German sugar beet test of the 1997/98 campaign showed a sugar yield of 6.24 tonnes per hectare compared with 6.07 tonnes in the second test of 1996/97, the sugar industry association WVZ said in a statement.</p>
<p>The test also showed an average sugar content of 15.0 percent compared with an identical 15.0 percent in the second 1996 test.</p>
<p>The second 1997 test was carried out on August 15.</p>
<p>The first 1997 test taken a fortnight ago showed a theoretical sugar yield of 3.93 tonnes per hectare and a sugar content of 12.6 percent.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
